    summary_en: "The EU has established a unified legal framework through the Cyber Resilience Act (Regulation n°2024/2847, abbreviated as CRA), aiming to enhance the cybersecurity of products containing digital components. This law requires manufacturers, importers, and distributors to implement cybersecurity requirements for products throughout their entire lifecycle, from the design phase. The CRA includes necessary cybersecurity requirements for the product itself and for vulnerability management, and introduces a conformity assessment procedure. Products complying with the CRA will bear the CE marking. The goal of this law is to ensure responsible operation across relevant industrial chains and boost consumer confidence in digital products. Practically, manufacturers must establish comprehensive security management systems to meet the stringent regulatory demands.",
